    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d819">

                <pb facs="1288" n="1274" xml:id="pg1274"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War/1258</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-19">January 19,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received January 19—7:32 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>514. From Pell. Following conference at Foreign Office, Commission was organized
                    formally at meeting held January 18. Rules of organization and procedure were
                    adopted. Foreign Office ready to drop proposed technical committee provided
                    governments concur. All members agree that Commission is adequate. Consensus is
                    that Commission should take broad view of functions and make recommendations to
                    governments on means of enforcement, including choice of tribunals. Refer to
                    Embassy’s 8504, December 6 [<hi rendition="#italic">7</hi>] and your 8229
                    December 30.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d819-f1"/> Request authorization that Mr.
                        Preuss<anchor n="12" xml:id="d819-f2"/> act as alternate at any meeting or
                    part thereof. Detailed report follows.<anchor n="13" xml:id="d819-f3"/>
                    [Pell.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d819-f1" n="11" xml:id="d819-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <ref target="frus1943v01#pg_432">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1943, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, pp. 432</ref> and <ref
                        target="frus1943v01#pg_435">435</ref>, respectively.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d819-f2" n="12" xml:id="d819-f2-content">
                <p>Lawrence Preuss, divisional assistant (legal) in the Division of International
                    Security and Organization; detailed to assist the American representative on the
                    United Nations War Crimes Commission until April 1944.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d819-f3" n="13" xml:id="d819-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
